.SH NAME
CWE\-610 \- Externally Controlled Reference to a Resource in Another Sphere
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product uses an externally controlled name or reference that resolves to a resource that is outside of the intended control sphere.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB2\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2022\-27593
QNAP Photo Station, added 2022\-09\-08, ransomware: Known.
.PP
QNAP Photo Station Externally Controlled Reference Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Certain QNAP NAS running Photo Station with internet exposure contain an externally controlled reference to a resource vulnerability which can allow an attacker to modify system files. This vulnerability was observed being utilized in a Deadbolt ransomware campaign.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-09\-29.
.PP
